2. Extract every RAML field (build the "RAML table")

Walk the RAML type tree recursively. For every leaf property (not container objects), emit one record with:

raml_path — full dotted path from root, using the exact property key names (never the description), appending [] for every array level it passed through (e.g. coreRisk.cover[].optionalExtras.courtesyCarTotalRepair, coreRisk.drivers[].occupations[].occupation_Occupation_Code). This is always built from the key, regardless of what happens in §4 below.
raml_key — the property's own key, exact case.
raml_description — the raw value of the description: attribute, or None if the key has no description at all.
raml_name — this is not simply "description if present, else key." Apply this 3-way classification (in order):
No description at all (raml_description is None) → raml_name = "Not Present". Note reason: "Description is not mentioned in RAML file".
Description equals the key, case-insensitively (i.e. identical once both are lowercased — this covers exact matches and pure-casing differences like buildingName vs BuildingName) → raml_name = raml_key (use the key's own casing). No mismatch is flagged for this case, even though the raw strings differ in case.
Description looks like natural-language prose — heuristic: it contains a period, or a comma followed by a lowercase word, or 4+ whitespace-separated words, or common sentence glue-words ("and", "the", "is", "during", "originally", "applicable", etc.) → treat it as a real explanatory description, not a name. raml_name = raml_key. No mismatch flagged. (Example: cacheID's description "cacheID, applicable during requotes and mid term adjustments..." falls here — display just cacheID.)
Otherwise — description is a short identifier-like string that genuinely differs from the key (pluralization, an inserted word, or a wholly different token) → raml_name = raml_description as-is, and flag a mismatch:
if raml_description contains a space → note reason "Field name mismatch"
if it does not contain a space → note reason "Tag name mismatch"
raml_type — the type: value, normalized as follows (case-insensitive, trim whitespace), and this normalized form is what gets printed in the output column (the manual reference report displays the normalized type, not the raw RAML/mapping text — e.g. it shows date in the cell, never date-only):
date-only → date
time-only → time
int → integer
everything else kept as-is (string, number, boolean, integer).
number and double are never synonyms of each other — keep them distinct.
raml_required — the required: boolean, exactly as written (true/false). If absent, treat as blank/unknown, not false.
3. Extract every mapping-document field (build the "Mapping table")

For every data row in MQS_Quote_Request (row 8 onward, skip blank rows):

map_path = column B, exact string.
map_name = column C, exact string.
map_type = column E, normalized the same way as raml_type above (same synonym table) — print the normalized value, not the raw one, same as the RAML side.
map_mandatory = column F, exact string (Mandatory / Optional). If the cell is blank/empty, set map_mandatory = "Not present" — the reference report never leaves this column visually blank; a blank source cell is always rendered as the literal text Not present.
4. Match RAML records to Mapping records

Match primarily by exact path (raml_path == map_path, case-sensitive). This is the normal case and covers the large majority of rows.

Produce one output row per union of matched pairs plus any unmatched leftovers on either side:

Matched pair (path found on both sides) → proceed to §5.
In mapping doc only, no RAML path found at all → raml_path = None, raml_name = "Not Present". Note text: see §6, case "path missing entirely."
In RAML only, no mapping row found at all → map_name = "Not present", everything else on the mapping side blank. Note: "Not present in mapping document".
A block/path that appears more than once in the RAML (duplicated structure, one correct + one erroneous) — do not try to auto-resolve which is correct. Emit a row flagged NEEDS MANUAL REVIEW — duplicate block in RAML instead of guessing (see §8, this is one of the two rows that required human judgment in the reference report).
